    "knowledge_point": "Differentiating a Quotient Using Leibniz Notation",
    "problem": "Given that $y=\\frac{-x}{9-2x}$, find $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}.$",
    "worked_solution": "Let $u=-x$ and $v=9-2x.$ Then\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x} & =-1\\,\\text{and}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the quotient rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{v\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}-u\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}}{{v}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{(9-2x)\\cdot (-1)-(-x)\\cdot (-2)}{{(9-2x)}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{-9+2x-2x}{{(9-2x)}^{2}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{9}{{(9-2x)}^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
